# Overfit Lab: how many backtests survive honest testing?

**Headline.** Of {{e3.n_variants:,}} trading-strategy variants backtested on {{e3.n_assets}} crypto assets ({{e3.data.start}} to {{e3.data.end}}, net of costs), {{e3.net.survivors.naive:,}} look significant when tested one at a time at 5%, {{e3.net.survivors.bh:,}} survive Benjamini-Hochberg, and **{{e3.net.survivors.holm:,}} survive Holm**.
The best variant has an annualised Sharpe ratio of {{e3.net.sharpe.best_annual:.2f}}, but luck alone is expected to produce {{e3.net.dsr_primary.sr0_annual:.2f}}: its **Deflated Sharpe Ratio is {{e3.net.dsr_primary.dsr:.2f}}** (0.95 needed), Hansen's SPA p-value is {{e3.net.snooping.spa_p:.2f}}, and the **Probability of Backtest Overfitting is {{e3.net.pbo.pbo:.2f}}**.
Measured against simply holding each coin, {{e3.vs_buy_hold.survivors.naive:,}} variants are significant even before any correction. Data: {{e3.data.label}}.

